Public keys (minisign, *.pub) that releases of TitanOS must be signed with.

An update is installed only if the manifest of the release carries a valid
signature of one of the keys in this directory. An image without a key
installs no updates at all.

The first published image must contain distinct release and offline recovery
public keys. Neither private key belongs in this repository. Keep the recovery
secret offline; only the release secret goes into the protected release
environment. More keys may be added during rotation: an update that adds the
new key is signed with an existing trusted key before switching signers.

rehearsal.pub is a disposable test key, ignored by Git. Tag builds reject it.

Configured public keys (2026-10-14):
  titanos-release-1.pub   Minisign key ID 8EAABC2A42904C1D
  titanos-recovery-1.pub  Minisign key ID E58A91B20B598ABB
Added during rotation (2026-11-03, TitanOS 0.46.2):
  titanos-release-2.pub   Minisign key ID 10239C7F77392DC9
  The private part of titanos-release-1 was no longer found; 0.46.2 is still
  signed with it and teaches the NAS the new key. Releases after 0.46.2 are
  signed with titanos-release-2. titanos-release-1 is removed in a later
  version.

Both key pairs have been verified locally. The release secret is configured
in GitHub's protected release environment. The project owner confirmed an
external backup of the keys and passphrases on 2026-10-14. Offline custody
of the recovery secret is still unconfirmed; a cloud copy is not offline.

See docs/RELEASING.md in the repository.
